# Vitest's scratch dir for toMatchScreenshot mismatch / missing-reference debug
# images. Never the committed baselines themselves (see below).
.vitest-attachments/

# Vitest browser-mode FAILURE screenshots. These land in a dir named after the
# failing test file, so a tier-2 (`<Name>.test.tsx`) capture is throwaway debug
# output while the real baselines live under `<Name>.visual.test.tsx/` and must
# stay tracked. The patterns match FILES rather than dirs so the negation can
# re-include — git cannot re-include anything under an excluded directory.
src/recipes/**/__screenshots__/*.test.tsx/*.png
!src/recipes/**/__screenshots__/*.visual.test.tsx/*.png

# NOTE the one place this deviates from soribashi's .gitignore, which it is
# otherwise a copy of: soribashi additionally ignores `*-darwin.png` /
# `*-win32.png` baselines, because its visual baselines are generated on Linux
# in CI and a local-platform capture there is advisory noise. This kit has no
# CI, so the platform-suffixed baseline a developer generates IS the baseline
# and is tracked. Revisit if the kit ever grows a CI pipeline.
